pdf.js 6.4.299 (Mozilla, Apache-2.0), vendored from the pdfjs-dist npm package so the PDF viewer
works offline. From the package:

  legacy/build/pdf.min.mjs, legacy/build/pdf.worker.min.mjs
      the legacy build, which also runs in older Safari / iPadOS versions
  web/pdf_viewer.css, and the web/images/ files it refers to
  wasm/      the JPEG 2000, JBIG2 and colour-profile decoders with their licences
             (openjpeg, jbig2 and qcms .wasm, the *_nowasm_fallback.js files, LICENSE_*);
             not quickjs-eval, which only runs a PDF's own JavaScript (the viewer never does)
  standard_fonts/, iccs/

pdf.min.d.mts is ours: it gives pdf.min.mjs the package's types (frontend/package.json installs
pdfjs-dist at the same version). The viewer passes wasm/, iccs/ and standard_fonts/ to getDocument
(frontend/src/viewer/viewer.ts).
